// Rule: [NO-MITRE-MAPPING] Darklantern - UDP 9992 Firewall Visibility
// MITRE ATT&CK: NO-MITRE-MAPPING
// Classification: Validation query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Sentinel / Log Analytics
// Required telemetry: CommonSecurityLog
// Purpose: Firewall telemetry validation for traffic directed to the source-documented router backdoor listener. Port metadata is not proof of probe, command execution, implant presence...
// Logic: Evaluate CommonSecurityLog for udp 9992 firewall visibility using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in CommonSecurityLog; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: the 19-byte probe, command packet, device response, implant presence, or compromise.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// DARKLANTERN inbound UDP/9992 firewall visibility
// Classification: Validation query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Platform: Microsoft Sentinel / Log Analytics
// Prerequisite: perimeter firewall traffic logs mapped to CommonSecurityLog through CEF via AMA.
// Purpose: validate whether the environment can observe traffic to the source-documented listener.
// A match does not prove the 19-byte probe, command packet, device response, implant presence, or compromise.

CommonSecurityLog
| where Protocol =~ "UDP"
| where DestinationPort == 9992
| project TimeGenerated,
          DeviceVendor, DeviceProduct, DeviceName,
          CommunicationDirection,
          SourceIP, SourcePort,
          DestinationIP, DestinationPort,
          DestinationTranslatedAddress, DestinationTranslatedPort,
          Protocol, DeviceAction, SimplifiedDeviceAction,
          DeviceInboundInterface, DeviceOutboundInterface,
          Message
| order by TimeGenerated desc
